 { If it is Black's turn, his king gets a dominant position and forces a favourable pawn exchange. After getting rid of the non-blocked pawn, Black captures the blocked pawn and wins. The procedure is very simple: } Kh4 2. Kf2 Kh3 3. Kg1 g3 4. hxg3 ( 4. Kh1 { would be an interesting attempt, but } Kg4 { leads to the same conclusion. } ) 
Kxg3 $19 { The black king has reached the key squares for the d3 pawn, so he will capture it and promote his pawn. } 
